# Use LSAN_OPTIONS="suppressions=../san.supp:print_suppressions=1" ./app

# pthread_once initialization frame (glibc)
leak:^__pthread_once_slow$
leak:nptl/pthread_once.c

# Vulkan loader: loading a layer or a driver `dlopen`s it, and that library's own static initialisers
# allocate process-lifetime state the loader never frees. The allocation therefore sits under the loader's
# open path and has no project frame - which is the discriminator: a leak that reaches project code has no
# loader frame and is still reported (#103). `print_suppressions=1` names each suppressed hit, so the
# remaining count is visible rather than silent.
leak:loader_open_layer_file
leak:loader_platform_open_library

# The driver module's own registration path, which is the leak that survives the loader frames on some
# machines: the NVIDIA driver reaches libdbus (`dbus_bus_register`) through `dlopen`, and AMDVLK allocates
# inside its own module. Module-scoped rather than `leak:*`, so a project leak has no such frame and is
# still reported. A driver built without symbols still reports as `<unknown module>` and cannot be matched;
# the acceptance is "no project frames in the report", not "a clean exit on every machine".
leak:libdbus-1.so
leak:amdvlk64.so
leak:libdrm.so.2

# The loader's terminator physical-device setup, called from `vkCreateInstance` through
# `loader_create_instance_chain` -> `terminator_EnumeratePhysicalDevices`. It asks each ICD to enumerate
# devices and keeps the returned lists for the instance's lifetime; on the CI software device (llvmpipe
# via SDK loader 1.4.363) one allocation per instance is still unreachable at exit, and with a fixture
# creating an instance per test that is dozens of reports (#189). The allocation is inside the
# uninstrumented ICD, so the frames above this one are module-less - this loader frame is the only
# discriminator, and a leak that reaches project code cannot contain it. The indirect thread-rooted
# blocks LSan reports alongside these are children of the same roots; suppressing the root removes the
# group (measured with a synthetic parent/child leak under these options).
leak:setup_loader_term_phys_devs
